{"UsernameForm calls isConditionalPasskeysEnabled() without arguments, but the only available method is isConditionalPasskeysEnabled(UserModel user) in UsernamePasswordForm. This won't compile. Update the call to pass the appropriate user or add a no-arg overload that delegates appropriately": 0.705999493598938, "isConditionalPasskeysEnabled currently requires user != null, which prevents WebAuthnConditionalUIAuthenticator.fillContextForm() from running on the initial login page (where context.getUser() is typically null). That means enableWebAuthnConditionalUI/challenge/rpId won't be set and the passkeys conditional UI form won't be rendered. Consider removing the user != null requirement or splitting the logic": 0.7780530452728271, "Typo in comment: 'Succesful event' should be 'Successful event'": 0.5016024112701416, "Checking for absence of //form[@id='webauth'] via findElement + broad Exception catch is brittle. Use Assert.assertThrows(NoSuchElementException.class, ...) or findElements(...).isEmpty() so the assertion is explicit and doesn't mask other exceptions": 0.7509444355964661, "Unused import: PasswordCredentialModel is imported but not referenced anywhere in this test class. Please remove it to keep the test compiling cleanly under strict build/checkstyle settings": 0.24815037846565247, "The test asserts that the WebAuthn form is not present by calling driver.findElement(...) and catching a broad Exception. Since findElement never returns null (it throws when missing), this pattern is brittle and can hide unrelated failures. Prefer Assert.assertThrows(NoSuchElementException.class, ...) or use findElements(...).isEmpty() to check absence explicitly": 0.7475160360336304, "This method overrides WebAuthnAuthenticator.shouldShowWebAuthnAuthenticators; it is advisable to add an Override annotation": 0.21425464749336243}